; Plan 04's RULE 2 in a `.mid`, with every hash agreeing.
;
; `song.mid` was written by `tempura build` from a one-lane native
; document (`tools/gen_fixtures.zig`, `residue_doc`) and nothing has
; touched it since, so the dump restores the AUTHOR's text — comment,
; title, `:qpm 120` spelling and all — rather than deriving a skeleton
; from what the file uses.
;
; `(reconciled …)` in the golden is the verdict table: the rule that ran,
; the conductor record's hash and one line per lane record. `restored`
; with `:hash-ok true` everywhere is what "the file and the document were
; written together" looks like.
(read)
(dump)
